     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Having family: います",
     "texto": [
      "To say you have siblings, **います** is used («there is», for people and animals), and what there is takes the particle **が**: **あね が います** (I have an older sister; literally «there is older sister»).",
      "Negative: **いません**: **いもうと は いません** (I don't have a younger sister).",
      "People are counted with a special counter: **ひとり** (one person), **ふたり** (two), and from three on, number + **にん**: **さんにん**, **よにん**, **ごにん**.",
      "**と** links nouns: **ちち と はは** (my father and my mother)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
